SUMMARY:Embodied Garden: 8-Week Art Therapy Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Join Mahja Kabir\, an artist and art therapy trainee\, for an eight-week closed art therapy group for adults!\nEmbodied Garden invites participants to slow down\, connect with nature\, and explore their inner world through creative expression. Each session includes a brief embodiment meditation\, gentle check-in\, nature-inspired art-making\, and optional sharing.\n \nAcross the eight weeks\, the garden becomes both a setting and a metaphor for exploring themes of grounding\, growth\, movement\, boundaries\, protection\, change\, community\, and belonging. Each session introduces a distinct theme while contributing to an overarching exploration of embodiment\, connection\, and our relationship with the natural world.\n \nAs a closed group\, participants are invited to attend all eight sessions. The continuity of the series offers opportunities to build trust\, develop connections\, and reflect more deeply as the sessions unfold.\n \nThe group is facilitated by Mahja Kabir\, an artist and art therapy trainee who creates gentle\, creative spaces that support reflection\, care\, growth\, and connection. Art therapy uses the creative process as a way to explore emotions\, experiences\, relationships\, and self-awareness\, with no emphasis on artistic skill or producing a finished artwork.\n \nWednesdays\, October 21 through December 9\, 10 a.m. to 12 p.m. (eight sessions).\nPublic $160\, TBG Members $120 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\n \nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/embodied-garden-8-week-art-therapy-workshop/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Ave E\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Art,Wellness
