SUMMARY:Botanical Printed Notebook and Prints
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a fun-filled afternoon of creating a customized notebook and prints!\nUsing the process of linocut\, you’ll create a custom printed Japanese notebook and 4 fine art prints. From designing your image\, through to carving and printing\, our instructor will demonstrate linocut techniques and provide individual guidance. By the end of the workshop\, you’ll leave with 1 unique botanical-themed notebook\, 4 original prints and new printmaking skills. Beginners welcome.\n \nYou can create anything\, so please bring photos\, sketches\, and designs for reference and inspiration. Your image needs to measure 4×6 inches. If you’re stuck for ideas\, pressed leaves will be available.\n \nMaking art can be messy\, please wear old clothes or an apron. Materials included.\n \nEach student will receive:\n \n\n\n1 Japanese notebook\n1 block of soft cut lino\n4 sheets of toned art paper\nblack printmaking ink\n\n\nSaturday\, October 24\, 1 to 4 p.m.\nPublic $80\, TBG Members $70 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Alan Li\nArtist and conservationist Alan Li uses pencils\, ink and paint to document the wonders of the natural world. Alan’s mission is to build connections to nature through arts-based education. Since 2015\, he has been partnering with non-profit environmental organizations to teach nature-focused art programs and workshops.\n \nAlan was responsible for the successful launch of the Toronto Nature Sketch program in 2018\, teaching all of the art lessons during that inaugural year. Nature Sketch is an initiative of Canadian artist Robert Bateman and the Bateman Foundation.\n \nIn 2019\, Alan was a speaker at the annual Ravine Symposium at Toronto Botanical Garden. In his presentation\, he shared stories behind ravine inspired artwork created by himself and a small brigade of volunteer artists. Funds raised through the sale of the artwork were donated to ravine conservation initiatives at the garden.\n \nAlan currently teaches Field Sketching\, Nature Drawing and Linocut Printmaking at Toronto Botanical Garden and the High Park Nature Centre.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\n \nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/botanical-printed-notebook-and-prints/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Ave E\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Art
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/d19265a17832f25d3887c5b2d6c1df5e.jpg
