SUMMARY:Holiday Succulent Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Join us this holiday season and create a one-of-a-kind succulent!\nCelebrate the festive season with a delightful holiday-inspired succulent arranging workshop! In this creative and relaxing session\, you’ll design a beautiful succulent arrangement in a charming birch-lined tin planter—perfect for adding a touch of natural elegance to your holiday décor or gifting to someone special.\n \nGuided by a succulent expert\, you’ll learn tips and tricks for arranging succulents with a seasonal flair\, including techniques for layering textures\, balancing colours\, and incorporating winter-inspired accents.\n \nAll materials are provided\, including a birch-lined tin planter\, premium succulents\, specialty soil\, and care instruction cards to ensure your arrangement stays vibrant through the holiday season and beyond.\n \nJoin us for this festive workshop and leave with a stunning centrepiece that captures the warmth and beauty of the holidays!\n \nSaturday\, November 28\, 10 to 11 a.m.\nPublic $55\, TBG Members $50 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Canadian Succulents\nMolly is the owner and operator of the small business Canadian Succulents. Canadian Succulents creates floral arrangements using entirely succulents and cacti plants. They not only arrange and design all of the creations\, but also grow all the plants that can be found in them as well. They operate out of a greenhouse just northeast of the city\, where they grow over 300 varieties of succulents and cacti. They grow and create these designs for wedding centrepieces and favours\, corporate events and gifting\, and hotel and office greenery.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/holiday-succulent-workshop-2/
